            0.114,
            0.26,
            0.361,
            0.282
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.1 Introduction"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.293,
            0.886,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have learnt about algebraic expressions in earlier grades. In this chapter, we will learn about the special types of algebraic expressions called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "linear polynomials",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Let us first consider a few examples of algebraic expressions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.376,
            0.511,
            0.607
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Raju went to a shop where there were sealed boxes of different colours on sale. The shop owner told him that the red boxes have 4 pens each and the blue boxes have 5 pencils each. Now, if Raju bought x red boxes and y blue boxes, how can he quickly figure out the total quantity of pens and pencils? Also, if he got 3 extra pens free, how many pens and pencils did he get altogether?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.525,
            0.37,
            0.878,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.525,
                0.37,
                0.878,
                0.575
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_0_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.677,
                0.581,
                0.745,
                0.598
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 2.1"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.606,
            0.886,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe that x red boxes will have 4x pens and y blue boxes will have 5y pencils. Also, he got 3 extra pens free. Thus, the total number of pens and pencils is given by the algebraic expression 4x + 5y + 3. In this example, 4x, 5y and 3 are "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "terms",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the expression, x and y are letter-numbers, the numbers 4 and 5 are the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "coefficients",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of x and y, respectively, and 3 is a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "constant",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". From now onwards, we will use a widely used alternate word for letter-numbers: "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "variables",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Thus in the expression 4x + 5y + 3, we say that the variables used are x and y."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.764,
            0.887,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A rectangular garden of length l metres and width w metres has to be fenced and decorated. A wire fence is to be laid along the length costing `100 per metre and a wooden fence is to be built along the width costing `80 per metre. Special seeds have to be sown throughout the garden which will cost `50 per square metre."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
